    "body": "Hmm, throwing exception certainly wouldn't work well with pipes.\r\n\r\nI wonder we could make pipes reusable; allowing destination to be closed gracely so that the source side can still be piped to elsewhere. Could be more general than decompression specific and also could deal with \"exotic\" case you mentioned. But then it's not clear what would be done with the partially consumed chunk.",
