    "created_at": "2025-08-16T21:01:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-16T21:01:36Z",
    "body": "> In the special case of the packfile format, we could solve it with a mode which continues decompressing after it reaches the end.\n\nThis is not needed for Git packfiles. We only need some way to know how much data was 'consumed' so we can continue reading further data, which in this case would be the 'header' of the next object followed by its zlib-compressed data, and so on.",
